      "overallStrength": "A low-usage, high-efficiency finisher in a clearly-defined role — nearly all his offense comes from cuts, put-backs, and rolling to the rim, and he converts those chances well (64.6% at the rim). For a role player, that's an efficient, low-risk profile."
    },
    "weaknesses": {
      "worstArea": "Jump shooting — 20.0% FG on jump shots (5 attempts) and 25.0% on threes (4 attempts). Very small sample, but there's effectively no perimeter game showing yet.",
      "worstPlayType": "Miscellaneous Plays, mostly turnovers, graded Below Average (19th percentile, 0.300 PPP) — worth watching as his role grows, though volume is modest (10 possessions).",
      "overallWeakness": "He has no real shot-creation or perimeter shooting profile yet — everything productive he does is generated by cutting, rebounding, or rolling, not shot-making. That's fine for his current role but caps what he offers if used away from the basket.",
      "developmentTarget": "Given the shooting numbers are all very small-sample right now, the main development target is simply expanding his offensive role beyond finishing — a jump shot (even a limited one) would raise his ceiling, but there isn't enough volume yet to say whether that's a real weakness or just an untested part of his game."
